<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sahib I Giray</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1551">1551</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sahib I Giray was khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazan">Kazan</a> from 1521 to 1524 and khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> from 1532 to 1551. Installed in Crimea with Ottoman support, he used Ottoman troops and firearms to strengthen the khan's power over the great clans and built up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhchysarai">Bakhchysarai</a> as his capital, with its palace. He was deposed and killed in 1551 when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> replaced him with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devlet-i-giray">Devlet I Giray</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sahib-i-giray.jpg" alt="Sahib I Giray" width="320" height="597" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Russian manuscript illuminators, 1560-1570s … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Facial_Chronicle_-_b.20,_p._077.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
